	enum in java:
	
	* enum is a keyword in java which was introduced from JDK 1.5V.
	
	* It is similar to a class because class file will be created as well as our java compiler will 
	  automatically generate an equivalent class for the enum.
	
	* It is used to declare universal constants, all the universal constants must be separated by 
	  comma and is optional at the end.
	
	Example:
			public enum Color {
				RED, BLUE, PINK //public + static + final
			}
			
	* All the enum constants are by default public, static and final.
	
	* For every enum compiler will generate the following.class file.

	  An enum, we can define inside a class, outside of the class as well as inside the method.
	
	* At the time of compilation, automatically one static method is added by java compiler 
	  to the enum.class file to fetch all the enum constants, the return type of this method is enum array.
	
		public static enum[] values();
	
	* Every enum object contains two properties name and order position so java.lang.Enum class 
	  has provided a protected constructor to assign the name and order position of enum constant, 
	  the order position always starts from 0.
	
		public static final Color RED = new Color("RED", 0);
		public static final Color PINK = new Color("PINK", 1);
	
	* In order to find out the order position of an enum constant we can use ordinal method.
		public final int ordinal();
	
	* Every enum extends from java.lang. Enum class so enum cannot extend any other class as well as 
	  a class cannot extend an enum because enum is implicitly final.

	* enum cannot extend a class but it can implement multiple interfacses.

	* The first line of every enum is reserved for enum constant. If we want to write any other member inside enum then It must be after enum constant and; is compulsory.

	* As we know an enum is internally a class so we can write everthing like static & non static field, static and non static. method, static and non static block but all these members must be written after enum constant.

	* We can define constrauctor inside an enum but It must be private.

	* Every enum constant is by default object of type enum.

	* At the time of loading the enum constant, appropriate constrauctor will be executed automatically.

	* Enum is containng enum constants, so we can pass thses constants in switch statement.

	* We can compare two enum constants by using operator OR equals(Object obj) method of java.lang.Enum class.
	equals(Object obj) method is final and Internally it also uses operator only.

	* In java.lang. Enum class name() and ordinal() methods are final so we cannot override 
	hence we cannot change the name and order position of enum constants.
	
	
	
	
	